From 5705b4c558eca0d681fdc99af25958b5c2775b95 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dmitriy Andreychenko <dmitriy.andreychenko@flant.com>
Date: Wed, 16 Sep 2026 16:34:33 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] lb: least-conn backend selection algorithm

Select the backend with the fewest open connections, opted into per service
with service.cilium.io/lb-algorithm: least-conn. Plugs into upstream's
lb4_select_backend_id_custom() hook; a BPF timer does the scan off the packet
path and the conntrack GC rebuilds the counters after an agent restart.

The scan runs at once when it has been idle and is otherwise rate limited to
LEAST_CONN_TIMEOUT, which the measurements in bpf/lib/least_conn.h put at 3ms.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
